:'''Gepard:''' ...The monsters have gotten stronger somehow. I don't remember them being this difficult...
:'''Serval:''' Thank goodness we got here in time. If we'd arrived any later...
:'''Gepard:''' That's one brave little girl... You were like that at her age too.
:'''Serval:''' Huh? I wouldn't go that far &mdash; I only had Dad to deal with. He could be fierce, but nothing like the monsters here.
:'''Serval:''' Besides, my problem with him wasn't that he was a strict father...
:'''Serval:''' I just couldn't believe that he never lifted a finger to oppose Cocolia's order to seal the passageway...
:'''Serval:''' Vowing to protect the Underworlders in one breath, and then deciding they deserved to be abandoned in the next... "Family code of conduct" &mdash; what a joke.
:'''Gepard:''' Father was a soldier. He wasn't supposed to question the orders from his superiors...
:'''Gepard:''' ...Never mind. I know I sound like I'm defending him, and I don't want to make you angry. At least now we've got the chance to right the wrongs.
:'''Serval:''' Hmph, I'm angry just thinking about it. Looking back, I'm glad I left home early.
:'''Gepard:''' Running away doesn't solve the problem. It's been ages since you two had those fights, but you still can't let it go... You need to walk out of his shadow.
:'''Serval:''' ...
:'''Gepard:''' I'm not trying to change your mind. I just want to know that your choice to leave this planet is a result of having thought things through, not because you're trying to run away from something.
:'''Serval:''' My choice...
:'''Gepard:''' ...Sorry, I sound like Dad.
:'''Serval:''' *sigh* Don't worry about it. I get what you're trying to say, I do! It's just... I need some time.
